ideration is the unshown tiles. For example, if the player plays W1, they might be safe from being stolen if another player needs that tile. Looking at the unshown tiles, W1 has 2 remaining. So playing W1 is relatively safe. \n\nTherefore, the best action is to play W1.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing W1 allows forming potential chows in the W suit and a pung of B3, setting up for a high-scoring hand like Pure Straight or All Chows.  \nReason: Discarding W1 maintains flexibility for forming two chows (W234) and a pung of B3, while avoiding critical tiles for opponents.  \nAnswer: Play W1"}
